# Golden (Accompany, roadmap 9310, Phase 4e, docs/design/orchestrator-
# pipeline-extraction.md §3.6/§16.3-16.5, phase4-execution-plan.md 4e): the
# node-9310 feature itself -- the band under chords DETECTED FROM the
# imported melody, no scripted `chord`/`seq` steer anywhere in this script.
# `chord mode single` + `chord detect on` arm live piano->chord recognition
# (single-finger, scale-aware) on the SAME numeric port (1) `midi-source
# load` replays the melody thru on (Pipeline's new forward-flow, runtime/
# pipeline.hpp); as each melody note lands, chorddet recognizes it and steers
# FollowedContext (`"src":"detect"` in the `chord-followed` events below),
# and `style load basic`'s bass/drums/chord1 parts (arrangrr's OWN Arranger +
# ChordEngine, unchanged) resolve against whatever FollowedContext currently
# holds -- same-tick visible (D53). C4 (tick 0) recognizes as C major (the
# same chord the C-major key's own home chord happens to be, so bar 1's
# opening voicing does not visibly change); D4 (tick 1920) recognizes as Dm,
# and chord1's voicing audibly SWITCHES to D-F-A-C at that bar -- the
# concrete, undeniable proof the band followed a melody-derived chord, not a
# scripted one.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load basic
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
chord mode single
chord detect on
midi-source load components/midisrc/tests/fixtures/tiny.mid
transport start
advance 3000
quit
